<section class="before-after-section">
    <!-- HISTORICAL CONTEXT: WHY 2015 -->
    <div class="historical-note">
        <span class="year-badge">⚠️ 2015</span>
        <p>
            At 14nm, the cost per mm² of a monolithic die skyrocketed. TSMC's
            16nm FinFET wafers cost ~$8,000; a single defect on an 800mm² die
            meant throwing away a <strong>$10,000+</strong> chip. The industry was
            bleeding money, and Moore's Law was hitting a brick wall.
        </p>
    </div>

